Model sources:
========================================================================
The artifacts this release builds are derived from checkpoints published by:

- Qwen (https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B)
  The base weights every line here is built from, and the tokens, template and tokenizer every
  artifact carries. Apache License 2.0.

- unsloth (https://huggingface.co/unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4)
  The compressed-tensors NVFP4/FP8 checkpoint whose MLP codes the `nvfp4full` line imports and whose
  FP8 attention and linear-attention it re-encodes. Apache License 2.0.

- QUASAR-QAT (https://huggingface.co/QUASAR-QAT/Qwen3.8-27B-QUASAR-NVFP4)
  The quantization-aware-trained checkpoint the `nvfp4qat` line imports unchanged. Apache License 2.0.
  The method is described in QUASAR: Lowering the Loss Floor of Quantization-Aware Training with
  Loss-Aware Reconstruction, arXiv 2608.13966.

- NVIDIA (https://huggingface.co/nvidia/Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4)
  The ModelOpt checkpoint whose NVFP4 MLP codes and per-site activation scales the `nvidia` line uses,
  the scales being the product of NVIDIA's own Local-Hessian calibration. Apache License 2.0.

- UkisAI (https://huggingface.co/ukisai/Swift-Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4 and
  https://huggingface.co/ukisai/Swift-Qwen3.8-27b)
  The Swift fine-tune's quantized and BF16 exports. UkisAI's contribution, the fine-tuned weights, is
  licensed under the Swift Open License v1.0 rather than Apache-2.0: the model card makes personal,
  research, educational, evaluation and commercial use free below US$1,000,000 of annual recurring
  revenue and requires a separate Swift Enterprise License above it. That card also records that
  nothing in that licence limits rights in Qwen3.8-27B itself under Apache-2.0.

- z-lab (https://huggingface.co/z-lab/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2)
  The DFlash2 draft every artifact here carries, at the revision pinned in its artifact section.

The activation-divisor calibration in tools/convert/calibration.py uses the method and the committed
corpus of cometkim's `calibrate_nvfp4full.py`, so this port's measured divisors are directly comparable
with the profile that tool produced.

